<title>BRAZIL: Brazil IBGE cuts coffee cherry crop figure.</title>
<headline>Brazil IBGE cuts coffee cherry crop figure.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's coffee crop in 1997 should reach 2.46 million tonnes in cherry, down 3.22 percent from a forecast of 2.55 million tonnes issued at the end of June, the National Statistics Institute (IBGE) said.</p>
<p>The drop is due to an adjustment in production forecasts for Minas Gerais state, the IBGE said.</p>
<p>The most recent estimate also marks a 6.42 percent fall from the 2.64 million tonnes produed last year.</p>
<p>The IBGE issues its figure in cherry whereas other forecasts are normally in green coffee beans. Agronomists say there is no reliable formula to convert cherry estimates to beans.</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
